## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about runtime extensibility, hot-swapping strategies, and concurrency in a performance-critical component. It also probes how to design minimal interfaces and a registry to avoid touching core logic while enabling new eviction policies.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern for eviction decisions
- Registry and dynamic loading of policies
- Thread-safe policy swap and atomicity
- Observability of policy behavior and performance trade-offs

## Code Example

```javascript
class EvictionPolicy {
  onHit(key){ }
  onMiss(key){ }
  evict(entries, maxSize){ /* return keys to evict */ }
}
class Registry {
  constructor(){ this._map = new Map(); }
  register(name, factory){ this._map.set(name, factory); }
  create(name){ const f = this._map.get(name); return f ? f() : null; }
}
class Cache {
  constructor(){ this.policy = null; this.strategyLock = false; }
  setPolicy(p){ this.policy = p; }
  // ... onHit, onMiss delegate to policy
